Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:25:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] walk: an expression operator that may raise has an error
 completion

The walk read every expression operator as unable to fail: only a
variable read or an explicit `error` gave an error route, so
`try {expr {1/$d}} on error {...}` never entered its handler. An
arithmetic, bitwise, logical or list operator now adds an error
alternative from the state its operands left, unless its operands are
constants that evaluate; a comparison never raises; `&&`, `||` and
`?:` raise on an operand whose truth is not proved.

tclsh 8.6.18 / 9.0.4 / 9.1.0 with d = x: `/`, unary `-` and `&&` raise
into the handler (`info exists cv` is 1), `==` does not (0). 8.4.20:
`expr {$x + 1}` with x = abc raises, `expr {$x == 1}` gives 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
